00:01:50.940 --> 00:01:56.260
Inflation protected equity sleeves use companies with strong pricing power to offset rising

00:01:56.260 --> 00:02:03.320
input costs. Today's 6.5% PPI print highlights why investors should screen for firms that have

00:02:03.320 --> 00:02:09.500
historically passed costs to customers without volume loss. Start by pulling the last 8 quarters of

00:02:09.500 --> 00:02:15.500
gross margin data in your brokerage screener, then filter for names where margins expanded even as

00:02:15.500 --> 00:02:22.440
PPI rose above 5%. This approach worked best during the 2021-2022 inflation spike

00:02:22.440 --> 00:02:26.860
when staples outperform growth by 18 percentage points on average.

00:02:27.780 --> 00:02:32.100
The main risk is valuation compression if rate cuts arrive faster than expected.

00:02:32.800 --> 00:02:38.100
Build the sleeve inside a TFSA to shelter the dividends that often accompany these names.

