00:04:15.120 --> 00:04:20.280
That result fell short of the NASDAQ's roughly 1.5% gain over the same window,

00:04:20.740 --> 00:04:27.740
producing negative 1.33% alpha. The position held a narrow gain but lagged the broader market as

00:04:27.740 --> 00:04:34.080
rotation favored other sectors. The new rule requires both a fundamental catalyst and a volume spike

00:04:34.080 --> 00:04:38.020
above the 20-day average before committing capital to healthcare launches.

00:04:38.740 --> 00:04:42.740
That discipline around durability brings us to a bigger historical parallel.

00:04:43.660 --> 00:04:49.320
Imagine you bought a high-flying AI infrastructure name last month on the back of a single large

00:04:49.320 --> 00:04:54.620
contract announcement. Your order filled at the opening print but the stock gave back half

00:04:54.620 --> 00:04:58.900
the gain by month end because revenue visibility was thin beyond that one deal.

00:04:59.640 --> 00:05:07.240
The mechanism is identical to 1999 and 2000 when investors bought click stories with little free cash

00:05:07.240 --> 00:05:14.100
flow only to watch multiples collapse once growth slowed. The pro tip is to demand at least three years

00:05:14.100 --> 00:05:19.680
of visible revenue from existing customers before sizing above 3% of the portfolio.

00:05:20.720 --> 00:05:26.080
Professionals always run a simple discounted cash flow check on the incremental revenue before adding.

00:05:26.880 --> 00:05:32.220
The biggest mistake with AI stocks today is treating every revenue headline as proof of durability.

00:05:32.980 --> 00:05:38.920
Instead, always separate companies already generating positive operating cash flow from those

00:05:38.920 --> 00:05:43.880
still burning capital to chase market share. While we apply those filters manually,

